\ ff-test: lines
\ The FF_SAFE_MEM checks find the word heap an address lies in through an
\ index the arena keeps up to date as heaps are allocated, grown, trimmed
\ and freed. It used to be rebuilt and re-sorted after every change, so
\ defining words and checking addresses in turn took quadratic time.
\ Runs only in FF_SAFE_MEM builds.

: p 32 emit . ;
create cz 0 ,  here cz -  constant cell

\ A data word that grows while it is the newest allocation grows where
\ it lies, so an address into it stays good. It used to move, leaving
\ the address behind.
: fill 0 do i , loop ;
create t 1 ,
t
200 fill
@ p cr

\ One trimmed to its size ends there.
variable x
x cell + @
x @ p cr

\ The heap, and the xt, of a forgotten word are gone.
create u 5 ,  u  forget u
@
: gone ;  ' gone  forget gone
execute
clear
